  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1107 PM CDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nRiver flooding continues along the Big Blue and Turkey Creek, with \nthe crest approaching Beatrice. \n\nA shortwave trough dipping towards the Great Lakes region pulled a \nweak cold front through the forecast area this evening. A few \nshowers tried to bubble up along the boundary, but precip struggled \nto reach the surface through a dry sub-cloud layer. Temperatures \nsurged in the daytime sunshine, warming into the mid and upper 70s. \n\nMostly sunny conditions will prevail over the next few days, with \nhighs remaining in the 60s and 70s through Monday. A thermal ridge \nover the western CONUS will shift eastward by midweek, warming us \nback into at least the mid 70s.  While there remains a slight chance \nfor a few warm air advection showers Thursday into Friday, the \noverall forecast remains notably dry through the majority of the \nnext 7 days.",
